## Known traps

- **`tags_moved`'s fourth argument is `discarding`, not "has no receiver".** `effects::give` passes
  `receiver.is_none()` today, which is the same thing while `None` means only `GIVE 0`. It stops
  being the same thing the moment `Unprojectable` also has no receiver, and `tags_moved`'s tail
  (`effects.rs:1334`) drops the `can_be_given` filter on `discarding` - so the old expression would
  let a player give a monster to an ally. It must become `matches!(reach, GiveReach::Discard)`.
- **`ours_here` before `shown_here`.** Our own units are in `region.units` too. Reversed, every row
  of ours reads as another faction's, and `a_gift_to_another_factions_unit_in_this_hex_empties_the_giver`
  would pass while every ordinary gift silently stopped crediting its receiver.
- **`Selector::WholeUnit` is not a transfer.** `rules/give`: `GIVE [unit] UNIT` "gives the entire
  unit to the specified unit's faction" - a change of ownership, and nobody's holdings move.
  `apply_transfers` `continue`s on it before resolving the target (`:2102`) and `transfer` doubts it;
  neither changes here. It is also the rules' own answer to `ah-8lej`, so do not repurpose it.
- **`effects::Working::known_units` is report-wide.** It is `ah-bxgs`'s TRANSPORT question, which
  reaches across hexes, and it is *not* the test a GIVE needs. Reusing it would make
  `GIVE <a unit standing three hexes away>` read as `Unprojectable` and quietly destroy the goods.
  The new `shown_in_region` is a separate field for that reason.
- **`hex.units` is our own units; `hex.region.units` is everyone's.** `Hex::read` (`:1701`) filters
  on `own`. Every "shown here" closure in this bead must read the second, and every "ours" closure
  the first. This is the single distinction the whole bead rests on.
- **`position_of` and `hex.find` already know `new-{alias}`; `effects`' `by_alias` does not.** It is
  keyed `(region_id, alias)`, so `Working::index_in` strips the prefix back off. `formed_unit`
  (`effects.rs:520`) is where the spelling is minted and is the only place it should be written.
- **A silver guard placed below the class branch would be missed by every unit test here.**
  `silver.rs`'s `Intent::Give` arm handles `Selector::Class` first and `continue`s out of it
  (`:1347`-`:1371`), so `GIVE 9999 ALL ITEMS` would still defer the whole purse against a target that
  does not exist. `give_lands` goes at the very top of the arm, and
  `crates/core/tests/silver_agrees_with_the_warning.rs` is what catches it if it does not.
- **Twelve `Lookups` literals in `silver.rs`'s tests** need the new field, and it must default to
  `true` - what the column did before this bead - or existing assertions move for no reason.
- **`ah-vcp8.1` has landed** (closed, `crates/core/src/orders/items.rs` exists) and `ah-o7td` merged
