**`resolve_item` (`:4699`)** becomes the same call over the hex:

```rust
fn resolve_item(
    text: &str,
    hex: &Hex<'_>,
    actor: &Ordered<'_>,
    ruleset: Option<&Ruleset>,
) -> Option<String> {
    item_named(ruleset, text, || {
        actor
            .unit
            .items
            .iter()
            .chain(hex.units.iter().flat_map(|ordered| ordered.unit.items.iter()))
    })
}
```

Same order of authority as today - catalogue, then the actor's own list, then the rest of the hex -
and the item-major walk its doc comment warns about is gone.

**`names_the_same_item` (`:4730`) stays.** `resolve_item` was one of its three callers; the other
