/// [`PoolShare::Unknowable`] has no counterpart here, and neither does [`PoolOverrun`]: a guessed
/// headcount is handled by [`region_share_of`], and the navigator chose against any finding at all
/// (see **User-facing decisions**), so nothing is reported and there is no overruns argument.
fn production_shares_for(
    hex: &Hex<'_>,
    ruleset: Option<&Ruleset>,
) -> BTreeMap<String, Vec<i64>> {
```

Body, following `market_shares_for`'s shape:

1. `let mut wants: BTreeMap<String, Vec<i64>> = BTreeMap::new();`
2. For `(index, ordered)` over `hex.units.iter().enumerate()`:
   - the unit's **first** `Intent::Produce { item }`, via
     `ordered.intents.iter().find(|placed| matches!(placed.intent, Intent::Produce { .. }))`;
   - `let Some(tag) = resolve_item(item, hex, ordered, ruleset) else { continue };`, then
     `let tag = tag.to_ascii_uppercase();`
   - `let Some((_, recipe)) = producing_skill(ruleset, &tag, Some(&ordered.unit.skills)) else { continue };`
   - `if !recipe.inputs.is_empty() { continue; }` — manufacturing draws on no pool;
   - `if ruleset.is_some_and(|rules| carried_away(hex, ordered, rules).is_some()) { continue; }`
   - the hex's own figure: `hex.region.products.iter().find(|p| p.tag.eq_ignore_ascii_case(&tag))`;
     `continue` where there is none — a hex yielding none of it has nothing to divide, and
     `region_share_of` answers that case directly;
   - the ask: build the workforce exactly as the two pricing sites do, then take
     `plan_production(recipe, work, ordered.early_items(), RegionShare::Unlimited)` and read
     `.wanted`; `continue` on `None` or on `wanted <= 0`;
   - `wants.entry(tag).or_insert_with(|| vec![0; hex.units.len()])[index] = wanted;`
3. Map each entry through `split_pool(&claims, pool)` where `pool` is that tag's `Products` amount,
   and collect.

The workforce is built with **`ordered.early_men()`, `&ordered.unit.skills` and
`ordered.early_items()`** — the ledger's picture — and never `facts.late().men`. That is what makes
the two passes below agree; see **Known traps**.

**`region_share_of`, new, beside it — the one place the three answers are decided**, because the
ITEMS ledger and the SILVER column must not decide them differently (`ah-ycuj`):

```rust
/// What the region leaves one unit's `PRODUCE` of the goods `item` names.
///
/// One function, called by both surfaces, for the reason `workforce_for` is one (`ah-vtwn`): the
/// ITEMS ledger and the SILVER column price the same order twice through arms that share only
/// their inputs, and `crates/core/tests/silver_agrees_with_the_warning.rs` is what finds out when
/// they drift.
///
/// [`RegionShare::Unlimited`] for a recipe that takes materials, for a unit a vessel is carrying
/// away, for goods nothing could resolve, and where there is no ruleset - every case in which no
/// regional pool can be said to apply. [`RegionShare::NothingHere`] where the hex's `Products` line
/// names none of the goods. Otherwise this unit's settled [`RegionShare::Share`].
fn region_share_of(
    hex: &Hex<'_>,
    ordered: &Ordered<'_>,
    index: usize,
    item: &str,
    shares: &BTreeMap<String, Vec<i64>>,
    ruleset: Option<&Ruleset>,
) -> RegionShare;
```

Its body applies the same gates as `production_shares_for`'s loop, in this order: resolve the tag
(`Unlimited` on failure); find the recipe (`Unlimited` on failure); `recipe.inputs.is_empty()` or
`Unlimited`; `carried_away` is `Some` → `Unlimited`; the hex's `Products` entry is absent →
`NothingHere`; otherwise `Share(shares.get(&tag).and_then(|s| s.get(index)).copied().unwrap_or(0))`.

**A guessed headcount is what the last `unwrap_or` is for, and it is deliberate.** A producer whose
`unit.men_estimated` is true has a guessed ask, so `production_shares_for` still counts it and the
split is a guess for everybody in the hex. That is accepted rather than answered with an
`Unknowable`: primary production costs no silver, so there is no `SilverDoubt` for it to reach, the
ITEMS column has no way to render an unknowable quantity, and `men_estimated` is only ever true for
a unit the catalogue could not classify — which means no ruleset, which means no recipe and
`Unlimited` two gates earlier. Say so in the doc comment.

