## User-facing decisions

The whole interview, both rounds. Mockups, all committed to `docs/ui/`:
`docs/ui/ah-1t41-a-clear.html` (chosen), `docs/ui/ah-1t41-b-remember.html` (rejected),
`docs/ui/ah-1t41-r2-states.html` (round 2).

### Round 1 — the cure, and how wide the rule is

**Q1. Which cure?** Two variants were built and the navigator opened both.

- **Chosen — A, the box empties.** Changing the list empties the box; the text is gone and is
  retyped if wanted. Nothing is announced: no toast, no "filter cleared" line, no undo.
- **Rejected — B, each source remembers its own filter.** The box would empty on the way out and
  refill on the way back. Rejected because the box would then change under the player in *both*
  directions, so a filter typed three minutes ago and forgotten reproduces the original symptom on
  purpose; because it is a feature smuggled inside a bug fix, with a second tier of questions behind
  it (does the memory survive a reload, a new turn, the Army's deletion); and because it disagrees
  with its neighbour — `ah-1mpx.4` round 3 clears the multi-selection outright when the source
  changes rather than remembering one per source.

**Q2. Does selecting a different hex on the map clear it too, while *This hex* is the source?**
**Yes.** The navigator took the wider rule — "any list replacement clears it" — against the
recommendation, which had argued for keeping it so that filtering on a name and walking the hexes
could answer "where are my scouts". That sweep is knowingly given up: the box now empties on every
hex, and finding the same name in the next hex means typing it again.

**Q3. Clicking the rail entry you are already on.** **Keep.** Nothing happened, so nothing is
disturbed — and a double-click on an Army entry opens its rename editor, so clearing here would make
a slip destructive. This must hold for all three kinds of entry; today the two built-in ones already
ignore a re-click and an Army does not, and that asymmetry is what `listShown` removes.

**Q4. Does the sort reset alongside the filter?** **No.** A sort on Name or Men still means something
on any list, the sort already resets itself when the new source stops drawing the column it sorts on,
and changing it would be new behaviour rather than a bug fix.

### Round 2 — the three cases the wider rule reopened

Choosing "any list replacement" in Q2 made three further things arguable, each drawn both ways in
`docs/ui/ah-1t41-r2-states.html`:

**Q5. A new turn's report loads.** **Keep the filter.** Nothing was pointed at — data arrived. And it
is the moment a filter is most likely to be deliberate: filtering on `scout` and importing the next
turn is how a player sees that one of their two scouts is gone, and clearing would throw away the
comparison the box was set up for. Held in place by `listShown`'s signature, which cannot see the
report.

**Q6. A hex is clicked while an *Army* is the source.** **Keep the filter.** The list genuinely did
not change — only the rail's *This hex* count follows the map — and the map is exactly where a player
looks while reading an Army spread over five hexes. `ah-1mpx.2` settled that the table does not move,
and `armies.spec.ts:89` pins it.

**Q7. The Army being shown is deleted, and the table falls back to *This hex*.** **Clear the
filter.** A different list is on screen and the Army is gone; keeping the text would hide 91 of 92
units for no reason the player could name, which is the exact symptom this bead exists to end.

**Q8. Focus, since the sweep now costs a mouse trip — refocus the box after clearing?** **No.** Focus
stays wherever it was, so arrow keys still pan the map and Tab goes where it went. Stealing the caret
into a text box on every hex click would cost the map its keyboard to save the sweep one mouse trip.

### The words

**No string changes anywhere, and none are to be invented.** The box keeps its placeholder
`filter units…` and its `aria-label` `Filter units` exactly as at `UnitTableDock.tsx:560-561`. The
empty-state line `No unit matches that filter.` (line 662) and the header hint's `, N shown` suffix
are unchanged; they simply stop appearing once the box is empty. There is no announcement, no toast
and no undo for a cleared filter — that was Q1, and A is silent by construction.

### The full table of cases, as agreed

| What happens | Filter |
|---|---|
| Click a different rail entry (*This hex*, *All my units*, an Army) | **Cleared** |
| Click the rail entry already selected | Kept |
| Select a different hex while *This hex* is the source | **Cleared** |
| Select a different hex while *All my units* or an Army is the source | Kept |
| A new turn's report loads | Kept |
| The Army on screen is deleted; the table falls back to *This hex* | **Cleared** |
| Change map level, or open or close a game (the store nulls `selectedRegionId`) | **Cleared**, and correct — a different map is a different list |
| The sort column, the selected unit, column widths and order | Untouched |
| Focus | Untouched |

