Both running totals live for one hex's pass and are dropped with it: a `BTreeMap` local to
`forecast_unit`, and a private `Ledger` field that `ledger_for` builds and discards. No store, no
component and no persisted setting is touched. What crosses the Rust/TypeScript boundary is exactly
three things — one new `BuyAllCap` variant, one new `BuyAllShown` field, one new entry in
`codes::ALL` — and all three are generated: `cargo test -p atlantis-hud-core` rewrites
`packages/core-client/src/generated/{BuyAllCap,BuyAllShown}.ts` and
`packages/core-client/src/coreVocabulary.generated.ts`. The only hand-written TypeScript is the
sentence branch and the settings entry above.

