#### 2. `packages/ruleset/src/data.ts` — the scraper

Re-export and import `ControlCap` from `./generated/ControlCap` in the two blocks at `data.ts:13-26`
and `:28-43`, beside `CastOutput`.

Six new patterns, beside the existing creation ones at `data.ts:426-443`:

```ts
/** `averaging 200 percent`, `an average of 100 percent`, `at an average rate of 200 percent`. */
const CREATION_AVERAGED = /\baverag(?:ing|e of|e rate of)\b/i;
/** The nine summoning skills, from their prose rather than the normalised sentence. */
const CREATION_SUMMONED = /\b(?:may|can) summon\b|\bchance (?:of summoning|to summon)\b/i;
/** `control a total number of his skill level squared times 4 wolves`. */
const CONTROL_SQUARED_TIMES = /control a total number of (?:his|her|their|its) skill level squared times (\d+)/i;
/** `may control a number equal to his skill level minus 2, squared, times two`. */
const CONTROL_OFFSET_SQUARED = /control a number equal to (?:his|her|their|its) skill level minus (\d+), squared, times (two|three|four|\d+)/i;
/** `the total number of dragons that a mage may control at one time is equal to his skill level`. */
const CONTROL_EQUALS_LEVEL = /may control at one time is equal to (?:his|her|their|its) skill level/i;
/** `may only summon a balrog if one is not already under his control` - a flat cap of one. */
const CONTROL_ONLY_ONE = /may only summon [a-z ]+ if one is not already under (?:his|her|their|its) control/i;
/**
 * Any sentence about controlling a number, with the four shapes above taken out, so a page that
 * states a cap this parser cannot read stops the scrape rather than silently recording none - the
 * same posture `readCastCost` already takes for a cost clause naming no input.
 */
const CONTROL_STATED = /\b(?:may|can) control\b|\bunder (?:his|her|their|its) control\b/i;
```

`readCastCost` (`data.ts:452`) fills the three new fields on every `CastOutput` it builds from this
paragraph:

- `averaged` is `CREATION_AVERAGED.test(paragraph)`; `summoned` is `CREATION_SUMMONED.test(paragraph)`.
- `control` is the first of the four cap patterns that matches: `CONTROL_SQUARED_TIMES` →
  `{ multiplier: Number(m[1]), offset: 0, exponent: 2 }`; `CONTROL_OFFSET_SQUARED` →
  `{ multiplier: wordOrNumber(m[2]), offset: -Number(m[1]), exponent: 2 }`;
  `CONTROL_EQUALS_LEVEL` → `{ multiplier: 1, offset: 0, exponent: 1 }`; `CONTROL_ONLY_ONE` →
  `{ multiplier: 1, offset: 0, exponent: 0 }`. Otherwise `null`.
- If none of the four matched **but `CONTROL_STATED` does**, `throw new RulesetScrapeError(...)`
  naming the skill and the sentence, worded like the existing throw at `data.ts:443-445`.

`wordOrNumber` is a new private helper: `two` → 2, `three` → 3, `four` → 4, otherwise
`Number.parseInt`. It exists because `data/BIRD` alone spells its multiplier as a word.

**The `CONTROL_STATED` guard runs only when this paragraph stated a creation.** `data/BIRD` level 1
is about scouting and says "the mage can control small birds of the sky" while creating nothing;
checking it unconditionally throws on a paragraph that has no cap to read. Put the guard inside the
branch that has already found a creation.

`mergeCast` (`data.ts:617`) needs no change: it dedupes `creates` by tag and the new fields travel
on the entry.

