## Known traps

- **`GIVE ... ALL SILV` after a `BUY ALL` is the one case the two surfaces cannot be made to agree
  cheaply, and the plan buys out of it deliberately.** `forecast_unit` defers *both* orders and
  resolves them against a running total in document order (`Deferred::GiveAllSilver`,
  `silver.rs:1122`). The ledger resolves the gift **eagerly**, in `transfer`
  (`semantics.rs:2677`: `TransferShape::All { except } => (balance_of(…) - except).max(0)`). So a
  unit writing `buy all GRAI` and then `give 5512 all SILV` would have the gift take everything
  before the deferred purchase saw it, and the ITEMS cell would show no grain where the game gives
  grain — *worse* than today's honest ` + ?`. Hence the guard in `settle_buy_all` step 2. Written
  the other way round (`give` first) both surfaces leave nothing and agree, which is why the guard
  tests `placed.line > after` rather than merely "has one".
- **`counted_with_singular` says `"0 grain"`, not `"no grain"`** (`semantics.rs:4039`). That is why
  `Lookups::counted_or_none` exists. Do not change `counted_with_singular` — every other caller
  states a quantity rather than an absence.
- **The pluralisation must stay in the core.** TS gets `boughtNamed` and `marketNamed` already
  written, for the reason `castMadeNamed` is pre-counted (`unitTooltip.ts:224-226`): the unit does
  not hold these goods, so `countOf`'s naive `+ "s"` would produce "19 grains".
- **`SILVER_NOTES` prints every note that applies, not the first** (`unitTooltip.ts:803-808`).
  Two plans were agreed against the contract that replaced and both failed verification. The new
  note therefore cannot shadow or be shadowed by anything, and its position in the array is reading
  order only.
- **`unitTooltip.test.ts` enumerates `SILVER_NOTES`** — `SAID_BEFORE` (`:1127`) maps every note id
  to the sentence its own `example()` produces, and `:1174` asserts its keys are exactly the
  array's ids. Three further `it.each` blocks (`:1106`, `:1116`, `:1177`) run over every note, so
  the new `example()` must be a fixture the new `when` actually accepts, or those fail too.
- **`bd show` renders Markdown; read this plan back with `bd show ah-jown --json`.** The pretty
  renderer reflows the tables and the fenced blocks.
- **The generated TS is written by `cargo test`, not by hand**, via
  `#[cfg_attr(test, derive(ts_rs::TS), ts(export))]`, and gated by `scripts/checkGenerated.ts`
  inside `pnpm run check:fast`. Run `cargo test` once, then commit what appeared under
  `packages/core-client/src/generated/`.
- **`bd`, cargo and pnpm all find their configuration by walking up**, so branch in a worktree under
  `.cerebro/worktrees/` and nowhere else — a worktree outside the repository gets its own empty bead
  database and its own build directory.
- **Two other beads are in flight in `semantics.rs`** (`ah-dxfd.2`, `ah-ofpb.2`). Neither touches
  `buy`, `Deferred` or the deferred pass. Rebase on `main` before opening the PR and expect conflicts
  only in `Ledger`'s field list and `ledger_for`'s initialiser; **resolve them by keeping both
  fields, never by restructuring either bead's work.**
- **Never ask for an effect-level test in `packages/shared`** — that package has no jsdom by
