### Where state lives

`Ordered` owns the post-orders view of a unit — its skills, its headcount, and whether men joined —
for the whole of `review_turn`. `Ordered::unit` keeps pointing at the **reported** unit and is never
rewritten; that boundary is `ah-z73s.2`'s and it is what keeps the ledger, the Silver column and
`item_effects` on the figures they read today. Two passes write it, in the game's own phase order,
and every check reads it.

