## User-facing decisions

The navigator opened both initial mockups:

- Option A kept the existing warning shape and named the limiting race after the level. Rejected because the navigator preferred the restriction to read as the reason first.
- Option B led with what the limiting race cannot learn. Chosen.

The navigator then chose:

- preserve today's global-ceiling warning and completion behavior when race-limit data or classified composition is unavailable, rather than suppressing the warning/completion filter;
- name every limiting race when several tie, even when the sentence wraps, rather than saying `"some races in this unit"`;
- when a unit is already above its legal ceiling, name its actual level (`"already at level 3"`) rather than say `"already there"`;
- when the report supplies no plural for a race, say `"the human race cannot..."` rather than `"this unit's race cannot..."`;
- when the race ceiling equals the skill's global ceiling, name the global skill cap because the race did not reduce it.

Exact warning strings:

- race ceiling, at it: `"humans cannot learn observation past level 2, and this unit is already there"`;
- race ceiling, above it: `"humans cannot learn observation past level 2, and this unit is already at level 3"`;
- one limiting race in a mixed unit: `"wood elves cannot learn combat past level 2, and this unit is already there"`;
- two tied races: `"humans and wood elves cannot learn entertainment past level 2, and this unit is already there"`;
- three tied races: `"humans, wood elves, and high elves cannot learn entertainment past level 2, and this unit is already there"`;
- no known plural: `"the human race cannot learn observation past level 2, and this unit is already there"`;
- global ceiling, at it: `"observation stops at level 5 and this unit is already there"`;
- global ceiling, above it: `"observation stops at level 5 and this unit is already at level 6"`.

The existing setting title remains `"Study with nothing to learn"`. Its exact description becomes `"A unit ordered to study a skill that at least one of its races cannot learn any further."`

No control, focus behavior, shortcut, persistence, loading state, or cancel state changes. The checkbox remains keyboard-focusable, Space toggles it, and the setting persists immediately through the existing warning-toggle behavior. Messages and the setting description wrap rather than truncate at narrow widths. A skill at its applicable ceiling is absent from `STUDY` completion and returns when the current report composition or level permits further study.

Chosen mockup: `docs/ui/ah-9hp7.2-race-skill-ceilings.html`.

