## User-facing decisions

Settled with the navigator over three rounds plus a confirmation, against rendered pictures
generated from the real ruleset. `docs/ui/ah-geka-graph-order.html` is the chosen design, merged in
PR #779.

**Round 1 - which layout.** Four variants, each drawn as the whole graph with summon balrog, dragon
lore and create ring of invisibility lit in turn.

- A, today: alphabetical within a tier, boxes on rows.
- B, re-ordered within a tier, boxes still on rows. **Rejected.** This is the bead's own suggested
  fix and it does not work: summon balrog's lineage goes from 783px to 891px, because a 38-row tier
  and a 2-row tier cannot line up while every box is on a row. It does cut the tangle (31,401px ->
  25,056px of total vertical line-length), which is why it is worth knowing it was measured and
  rejected rather than overlooked.
- C, alphabetical order kept, boxes free to slide. **Rejected**, though it was close: 69 of 70
  lineages readable, and it keeps the one way a reader can find a skill by eye, since the graph has
  no search. The navigator preferred the straighter picture.
- **D, re-ordered and free to slide. Chosen.** 70 of 70.

**The cost the navigator accepted, in their words as it was put to them:** a column no longer reads
alphabetically, so a skill is found by following a line or by switching to the Branches view.

**Round 1 also asked** whether lighting a skill should move the view to fit its lineage. **Answer:
no, out of scope for this bead.** Lighting still only lights and dims; the reader pans and zooms by
hand, exactly as today. Do not add it, and do not add a "Fit lineage" button - that variant was
offered and declined.

**Round 2 - the tier headings.** Free heights mean three of the five columns start hundreds of units
below their heading, so a reader at the top of the drawing sees `FOUNDATIONS` with nothing under it.
Three variants: leave them; a hairline from each heading down its column; each heading moved down to
sit above its own first box. **Chosen: the hairline.** Moving the headings was rejected because the
five would no longer line up with each other.

**Round 2 - how wide a hole may get.** Three variants: no cap; no hole wider than three rows (81px);
no hole wider than one row (27px). All three keep 70 of 70 readable. **Chosen: no cap** - a box sits
exactly where the maths puts it. The navigator was asked again at the end, when the widest hole
turned out to be 313px and summon balrog's lineage 429px rather than the 243px quoted in round 2,
and confirmed no cap. **Do not add a cap.**

**Round 2 - manipulation.** It is the one skill with no prerequisite and nothing standing on it, so
nothing pulls it anywhere and it simply keeps whatever seed position it started from - which is
arbitrary and visible. Two variants: leave it wherever it lands; pin it at the foot of the
Foundations column. **Chosen: the foot.**

**Round 3 - how the hairline is drawn.** Four variants, all with summon balrog lit: in the gutter
8px left of the column stopping at the last box; in the gutter running the full height of the
drawing; down the middle of the column behind the boxes, showing only in the holes; and the gutter
one again but fading with the lit lineage. **Chosen: the gutter, stopping at the last box, and it
does not fade.** So its length tells a reader how far the tier reaches, it never passes behind
anything, and it behaves like the tier heading beside it rather than like a skill.

**Round 3 - how far apart manipulation sits.** Three variants: straight after spirit at the usual
5px; one blank row; two blank rows. **Chosen: one blank row** - `2 * ROW_PITCH` below spirit's top,
which is 32px of clear air between the boxes.

