`beginDrag` is a **local function inside `UnitTableDock.tsx`**, not a module of its own: it closes
over `pick`, `visible`, `armies`, `actions`, `dispatch` and `setDrag`, and threading six things
through a hook to save twenty lines would buy nothing testable — `packages/shared` cannot run a
pointer gesture in a unit test either way. Only the chip is extracted, because the chip is the part
that writes to the DOM and can be pinned without a pointer.

**Derived**, beside `visible` (`:296`):

```tsx
/** The unit numbers the table is drawing, in the order it is drawing them. */
