#### 5. `packages/shared/src/unitTable.ts` — edited

Three changes, and **`UNIT_COLUMNS` is not one of them.**

- `SortColumn` (line 34) gains `"seen"`. It is its own union, not derived from `UnitColumn`, so this
  is a one-word edit.
- `sortUnits` (line 271) gains a seventh parameter, in the shape the two before it already have:

  ```ts
  /** Each Army member's `seenTurn`, for the column that sorts on it. `ah-1mpx.2`. */
  seen: ReadonlyMap<string, number> = new Map()
  ```

  and `valueOf` gains its `"seen"` case, reading `seen.get(unit.unitId) ?? null`.
- One new export, which is what lets a column be hidden without the table going short:

  ```ts
  /**
   * The visible columns' shares, renormalised so they and the extra columns exactly fill the
   * table.
   *
   * `table-fixed` will not stretch to cover a gap, and the whole argument for shares over pixels
   * (see `ColumnShares`) is that the values always sum to 1. Hiding `faction` for one source, or
   * giving a fixed slice to a column that is not in `UNIT_COLUMNS` at all, breaks that unless the
   * remainder is scaled back up — so this is the one place a width is computed when the drawn set
   * is not the whole set.
   */
  export function sharesFor(
    visible: readonly UnitColumn[],
    shares: ColumnShares | null,
    /** Total share taken by columns outside `UNIT_COLUMNS`, between 0 and 1. */
    extra: number
  ): ColumnShares;
  ```

  Its result is passed to the existing `columnWidthStyle(column, …)`, which is unchanged.

**`UNIT_COLUMNS` stays at ten, and this is the central decision of the bead.** Adding `hex`, `seen`
and `remove` to it would reach `columnOrderFromStorage` (line 470), which rejects any stored order
whose length is not `UNIT_COLUMNS.length` — every existing user would silently lose the column order
they had arranged. It would also move `faction` and `men` in the default order, and the smoke suite
reads them positionally as `td:nth-child(4)` and `td:nth-child(5)`, and Silver as `td:last-child`
(see *Known traps*). Keeping the three new columns outside the persisted machinery means **the
`This hex` source renders exactly today's ten columns in today's order**, so every stored preference
and every existing test is untouched. The price is that the three new columns are fixed-width and
take no part in dragging or reordering — which is right anyway, since a stored width for a column
that is absent in most views would mean nothing.

The vocabulary and the shares are both declared in `unitTable.ts`, beside `UnitColumn` (line 62) and
`DEFAULT_COLUMN_SHARES` (line 351), against the same nominal 1440px table the latter is measured on.
**They live here rather than in `unitSource.ts` because `unitTable.ts` cannot import from it without
the two modules importing each other:**

```ts
/**
 * The source-dependent columns, drawn to the right of `name` in this order and deliberately NOT
 * members of `UNIT_COLUMNS` — see `sharesFor` for why.
 */
export type ExtraColumn = "hex" | "seen" | "remove";

/** Their shares. Fixed: these columns are neither dragged nor reordered nor stored. */
export const EXTRA_COLUMN_SHARES: Record<ExtraColumn, number> = {
  hex: 0.055,     // ~79px — `(11,55)` and its ellipsis
  seen: 0.052,    // ~75px — `turn 68`
  remove: 0.06    // ~86px — the Remove button
};
```

**Where they are drawn:** `hex` and `seen` immediately after the `name` column wherever `name` has
been dragged to, and `remove` always last, after every `UNIT_COLUMNS` entry. `hex` before `seen`
where both are present. That is `docs/ui/ah-1mpx.2-r5.html`'s drawing and
`docs/ui/ah-1mpx-r3.html`'s W1.

