## The test plan

**Rust unit tests**, inline in the two modules' own `mod tests`, named as the increments name them.
`silver.rs` gets the arithmetic (increments 1–3), `semantics.rs` the ledger, the settlement and every
sentence (4–11). The house style is a long snake_case sentence — `a_market_split_never_sells_more_than_the_line`,
`selling_horses_does_not_contend_with_selling_swords` — and a `/// ah-vw8e, increment N.` doc comment
above each, as `ah-q7jd`'s tests carry.

**Every message assertion is on the whole string**, `assert_eq!` against a literal, never a
`contains`. The shipped tests do this and it is what makes a wording change fail loudly.

**Fixtures** are the module's own builders: `region`, `ReportRegion { wanted: vec![MarketItem { … }], .. }`,
`unit("2390")`, `with_item(unit("2390"), 10, "furs", "FUR")`, `report`, `ruleset`, and orders as a
`&str` passed to `review_turn` with `CheckOptions::default()`. Copy
`a_sale_emptied_by_this_units_own_gift_is_warned_on_its_sell_line` (`semantics.rs:8977`) wholesale
and change the orders line.

**Corpus.** `crates/core/tests/silver_agrees_with_the_warning.rs` must stay green over all 26
fixtures. It is not extended here: it holds the column against the `not-enough-silver` warning, and
